## V7b/V7c batched decode — GO for Qwen3.5 CUDA

Profile ([archive](docs/benchmarks/archive/07-batched-decode.log)): a step is 24 ms,
66% weight-read-bound matmul; the N-token Q8 kernel did not share weight reads,
so an N-token variant of the one-token matvec was added (Qwen3.5 only).
`forward_batch` runs projections, norms, MLP and LM head over one row per
sequence, and convolution, recurrence, KV write and attention per sequence. The
gate gives the decode step at the front of the queue every waiting decode step
(at most 3) and lends the caches by value.

V7b staged a full copy per batch member (87 MiB at ctx 2048): +160–190 MiB, gate
missed. V7c ([archive](docs/benchmarks/archive/08-batched-memory.log)) writes
caches in place and, if a pass fails after writing, marks every cache in the batch
for replay from its token ledger. DeltaNet-only staging was rejected (no gain).

| Clients (128 tokens each) | V7 sequential | V7b | V7c | Per-stream events/s (V7 → V7c) |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 1 | 29.5 events/s | 29.7 | 29.3 | 31.8 → 31.8 |
| 2 | 29.1 | 45.1 | **44.5 (1.53x)** | 15.4 → 24.8 |
| 3 | 29.0 | 53.1 | **54.5 (1.88x)** | 10.2 → 20.4 |

Engine ceiling 1.00/1.79/2.35/2.80x for B = 1–4, logits bit-identical. VRAM at 3
decoders 4632–4696 MiB vs V7 4632–4792, V7b 4792–4856: growth <= 0 (gate 128
MiB), RSS +18–36 MiB. A missed wake-up made the leader sleep the full 4 ms
collection window each step; `notify_all` cut it to 0.48 ms (+3%). Vs V7: 3 short
clients TTFT p95 1.07 → 1.09 s, mean completion 2.05 → 1.60 s; long job 14.3 →
14.1 s; solo unchanged. Greedy text equals V7's in every run; a replayed cache
after a failed batch differs by 5.7e-6 in logits (same token, not bit-exact). HF
check, isolation, cancellation, sessions, CUDA/scalar tests hold.



